{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"As of **November 6, 2026**, [Rule 6c-11(d)](https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-17/section-270.6c-11) requires a US ETF relying on the rule to preserve:\n\n- **AP agreements:** All written agreements, or copies, between the ETF and authorized participants permitting purchases or redemptions of creation units.\n- **Each exchanged basket:** Records identifying each holding’s ticker symbol, CUSIP or other identifier; description; quantity; and percentage weight; any cash balancing amount; and the transacting AP’s identity.\n- **Custom baskets:** Where applicable, identification as a custom basket and a record stating that it complies with the ETF’s policies and procedures adopted under Rule 6c-11(c)(3).\n\n**Retention:** Both agreement and basket records must be maintained for **at least five years**, with the **first two years in an easily accessible place**.\n\n**Worth knowing:** The two-year accessibility period is included within—not added to—the five-year retention period."}}
